<Base title="How We Work | ITKeepers"><section class="section"><p class="eyebrow">How we work</p><h1>Know the environment.<br>Watch the signals.<br>Own the follow-through.</h1><p class="lead">The difference is not a tool list. It is how familiar engineers share context, escalate internally and stay involved.</p><p>Automated monitoring can surface issues continuously. Human coverage and response commitments depend on the service agreement.</p></section><Workflow id="how-workflow" /><section class="section light"><div class="split"><div><span class="illustrative-badge">Illustrative</span><h2>Daily checks.<br />Questions behind the work.</h2><p>These examples explain what a review can consider. They contain no client records, real alerts or promised schedule.</p></div><DailyChecks /></div></section><section class="section"><h2>Why these examples are illustrative.</h2><p class="lead">The storage warning and review questions explain a possible process. They are not a report from a client environment, a guarantee of response time or a promise that every incident follows every step.</p></section></Base>
